FILE: app/src/set-share.ts
```ts
import type { AnimationManager, AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { fadeAnimationWeight } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function setShareNow(manager: AnimationManager, group: AnimationGroup, share: number): void {
    group.weight = share;
    fadeAnimationWeight(manager, group, { to: share, durationMs: 0 });
}
```

I set the weight directly (which is unchecked per the notes) and then called `fadeAnimationWeight` with a zero-duration fade targeting the same value, which replaces any in-flight fade on that group (per note 13) so nothing will overwrite the weight on subsequent updates. The only thing I'm not fully certain of is whether the library handles `durationMs: 0` gracefully (e.g., no division-by-zero in its internal step calculation); if it does not, a one-frame fade (`durationMs: 1`) would be a safe substitute.
